# Locally-generated spaCy model artifacts (e.g. pruned models for memory
# testing). The exception is en_core_web_lg_pruned, which the deploy image
# actually runs on and is therefore tracked - the Dockerfile no longer builds
# it, because doing so peaks at ~1.28GB RSS and gets OOM-killed on a free-tier
# builder. Regenerate it with backend/scripts/build_pruned_model.py.
# Note this ignores the directory's contents, not the directory itself: git
# cannot re-include a path underneath an ignored directory.
backend/models/*
!backend/models/en_core_web_lg_pruned/

# Test files (scratch scripts at the repo root only - the real pytest
# suite in backend/tests/ is tracked, see the negations below)
test_*.txt
test_*.py
*_test.py
test_*.js
test_*.ts
*.test.js
*.test.ts
*.spec.js
*.spec.ts
!backend/tests/**

